' TimeUtil — shared calendar/clock helpers, extracted from LibraryStore so a
' screen can mint an ISO timestamp or gate an episode's airdate without reaching
' into a data store. Pure date logic (the only platform API is roDateTime inside
' NowIso), so it behaves identically in the interpreter test harness and on a
' device. Constructed once under MainScene scope and handed out through the
' stores map, like WatchedCodec — never built inside a method, or the
' per-component scope of user-defined globals would make the constructor resolve
' to invalid when invoked from a screen.

class TimeUtil
    ' Current UTC time in ISO-8601 transport format. "" when the platform clock
    ' is unavailable.
    function NowIso() as string
        try
            dt = CreateObject("roDateTime")
            if dt = invalid then return ""
            iso = dt.ToISOString()
            if iso = invalid then return ""
            return iso
        catch e
            return ""
        end try
    end function

    ' Whether an episode has aired: its release date (released, falling back to
    ' firstAired) must exist and not be after today. Dates compare on their
    ' leading YYYY-MM-DD (both UTC), so no platform date arithmetic is needed
    ' and the interpreter cannot diverge from a device. Missing/malformed dates
    ' or an unavailable clock (nowIso = "", or no roDateTime) are treated as
    ' aired — the goal is never to hide a claimable episode, only to block ones
    ' that demonstrably have not aired. That matters because an account bitfield
    ' for a series marked fully watched runs across the whole known episode
    ' list, including not-yet-aired placeholders; literally replaying those bits
    ' would paint a check on episodes that cannot have been watched.
    function EpisodeAired(ep as object, nowIso = invalid as dynamic) as boolean
        if ep = invalid then return true
        dateStr = ""
        if ep.released <> invalid and ep.released <> "" then
            dateStr = ep.released
        else if ep.firstAired <> invalid and ep.firstAired <> "" then
            dateStr = ep.firstAired
        end if
        if dateStr = "" then return true
        if nowIso = invalid or nowIso = "" then nowIso = m.NowIso()
        if nowIso = "" then return true
        day = dateStr.Mid(0, 10)
        if not m.IsCalendarDate(day) then return true
        if day > nowIso.Mid(0, 10) then return false
        return true
    end function

    ' YYYY-MM-DD shape check (the first ten characters of a date string), so a
    ' clearly non-date value can't accidentally compare greater than today.
    function IsCalendarDate(value as string) as boolean
        if value = invalid or value.Len() < 10 then return false
        digits = "0123456789"
        for i = 0 to 9
            c = value.Mid(i, 1)
            if i = 4 or i = 7
                if c <> "-" then return false
            else if digits.InStr(c) < 0
                return false
            end if
        end for
        return true
    end function
end class